{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 30,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "“But now they mock me, men younger than I am, whose fathers I would have refused to put with my sheep dogs.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What use to me was the strength of their hands, since their vigor had left them?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Gaunt from poverty and hunger, they gnawed the dry land, and the desolate wasteland by night.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They plucked mallow among the shrubs, and the roots of the broom tree were their food.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They were banished from among men, shouted at like thieves,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "so that they lived on the slopes of the wadis, among the rocks and in holes in the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They cried out among the shrubs and huddled beneath the nettles.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A senseless and nameless brood, they were driven off the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now they mock me in song; I have become a byword among them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They abhor me and keep far from me; they do not hesitate to spit in my face.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because God has unstrung my bow and afflicted me, they have cast off restraint in my presence.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The rabble arises at my right; they lay snares for my feet and build siege ramps against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They tear up my path; they profit from my destruction, with no one to restrain them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They advance as through a wide breach; through the ruins they keep rolling in.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Terrors are turned loose against me; they drive away my dignity as by the wind, and my prosperity has passed like a cloud.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now my soul is poured out within me; days of affliction grip me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Night pierces my bones, and my gnawing pains never rest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With great force He grasps my garment; He seizes me by the collar of my tunic.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He throws me into the mud, and I have become like dust and ashes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I cry out to You for help, but You do not answer; when I stand up, You merely look at me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You have ruthlessly turned on me; You oppose me with Your strong hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You snatch me up into the wind and drive me before it; You toss me about in the storm.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, I know that You will bring me down to death, to the place appointed for all the living.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet no one stretches out his hand against a ruined man when he cries for help in his distress.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have I not wept for those in trouble? Has my soul not grieved for the needy?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But when I hoped for good, evil came; when I looked for light, darkness fell.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am churning within and cannot rest; days of affliction confront me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I go about blackened, but not by the sun. I stand up in the assembly and cry for help.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have become a brother of jackals, a companion of ostriches.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My skin grows black and peels, and my bones burn with fever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:JOB.30.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My harp is tuned to mourning and my flute to the sound of weeping.[’’]",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
